            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Malayalam for to refund, then the Malayalam for an arrangement."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: സേവനം",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "സേവനം — sēvanaṁ — \"a service\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ആ ഹോട്ടലിലെ സേവനം വളരെ നല്ലതായിരുന്നു. ā hōṭṭalile sēvanaṁ vaḷare nallatāyirunnu. The service at that hotel was very good."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A bus service, a bank service and public service are all സേവനം (sēvanaṁ)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "സേവനം (sēvanaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit sevana, \"serving, attending on\", from the root sev, to serve (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
